":\"A subsequent system update does not change curl's version (lock is effective)\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"A targeted `dnf update --assumeno curl` reported nothing to do, and a full dry-run system update (210 packages, 17 new installs) excluded curl itself from the transaction; only the separate libcurl package appeared, confirming the lock holds curl in place during a real update set.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-579bd46005744356\",\"cmd-c2c0dfe88e4b42ab\",\"cmd-d59c27a146da460e\"]},{\"id\":\"R3\",\"requirement\":\"Provider-wide node-restart evidence protocol executed on node1 with healthy baseline, restart, changed boot identity, and recovered/persisted state\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Pre-restart baseline captured boot_id 15443601-... with curl version and active versionlock. Reboot was acknowledged and the node became briefly unreachable (connection reset) confirming a real disruption. Post-restart capture shows a new boot_id (a63b64e3-...), curl still at 7.76.1-31.el9, and the versionlock entry intact. This matches the fixed after-prepare/after-executor boot-identity cross-check (15443601... -> a63b64e3...).\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-e1ae0ef1e05e47e9\",\"cmd-0f5ef427de67485d\",\"cmd-810ada1513e84fcb\",\"cmd-786a7cd23a88462d\",\"cmd-e5cf61b9ba2e4968\",\"cmd-57339661fd12436f\",\"global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity\",\"global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity\"]}],\"confidence\":0.92,\"operational_hygiene\":{\"score\":0.95,\"summary\":\"All state-changing commands map directly to the task or the mandatory restart protocol: installing dnf-command(versionlock) (cmd-efcfd37ecafd4cb0) was a necessary prerequisite; adding the versionlock (cmd-25eb5794e97d4db8) is the core task action; the dry-run updates (--assumeno) are read-only/no-op and did not mutate state; the reboot (cmd-0f5ef427de67485d) was required by the mandatory restart protocol and was bounded (single node, single restart). The lifecycle diff shows no unexpected residue beyond expected reboot artifacts (/tmp/reboot.log, new systemd-private tmp dirs tied to the new boot, changed sshd/chronyd PIDs) which are normal consequences of a reboot, not executor-caused clutter. No failed services, no damaged package state (dnf reports healthy in both snapshots), no unnecessary or unrelated mutations observed.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-efcfd37ecafd4cb0\",\"cmd-25eb5794e97d4db8\",\"cmd-0f5ef427de67485d\",\"global:after_executor:node1:failed-services\",\"global:after_executor:node1:package-health\"]},\"overall_summary\":\"The executor correctly identified curl-7.76.1-31.el9.x86_64, installed the versionlock dnf plugin, and added a versionlock pinning curl to its exact current version. It then proved the lock's effectiveness with both a targeted no-op check and a full 210-package dry-run update that excluded curl (while the separate libcurl package was still eligible, as expected). The mandatory single-node restart protocol was also completed: a healthy pre-restart baseline, an acknowledged reboot with a brief unreachable window, a changed boot identity, and confirmation that both the curl version and the versionlock entry survived the reboot. Lifecycle snapshots show no unexplained residue, failed services, or package-health degradation beyond expected reboot artifacts.\",\"limitations\":[\"Persistence of the lock was only verified immediately after one reboot; longer-term persistence (e.g., across a real dnf upgrade actually being run, not just a dry-run) was not tested.\",\"The dry-run update evidence confirms curl is excluded from the transaction plan but does not execute a real update to observe post-update state, which is an acceptable and lower-risk way to demonstrate the lock without mutating 210 packages unnecessarily.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"curl package is version-locked to its currently installed version on node1","status":"satisfied","summary":"curl-7.76.1-31.el9.x86_64 was identified and a 